ki::mtls"},{"text":" needs to authenticate an IoT device or a service","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"account by certificate rather than by secret. # What is and is not copied Only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public_cert_pem"},{"text":" — the certificate. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"private key stays where its custodian put"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it"}]},{"text":" (Vault, or sealed into the row) and is never written to the server volume. A trust","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anchor is public by construction: it is what the server hands every client during the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"TLS handshake, and every device that has to validate the chain already holds a copy. #","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Why a restart rustls builds its ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootCertStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once, when the listener is constructed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and actix-web binds that config for the process’s life. Toggling this changes what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"next"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" boot trusts, and the API says so in its response rather than pretending the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change took effect. Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a deployment that never touches this keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly the TLS posture it has today.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mtlsTrustAnchor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"mtlsTrustAnchor","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/